    56	## The seven units
    57	
    58	Each unit names its stipulated objects first. The stipulation is the
    59	boundary of the claim: nothing about physical records, readouts,
    60	masses, angles, or lattice dynamics follows from any of it.
    61	
    62	### 1. Trace-free/conformal split of a sector triple
    63	
    64	Stipulated: a sector triple is a vector v in Q^3; the conformal
    65	channel is conf(v) = (trace(v)/3)(1,1,1); the trace-free channel is
    66	tf(v) = v - conf(v); the graded operator is
    67	G_sigma(v) = tf(v) + sigma*conf(v); the recoil ledger family is
    68	(-2w, w, w) for integer w.
    69	
    70	Exact results: tf + conf = id; trace(tf(v)) = 0; the two projectors
    71	are idempotent, complementary, and mutually annihilating; the
    72	constant part of the split is unique; every ledger triple (-2w, w, w)
    73	has sector trace zero, so its conformal channel vanishes and every
    74	G_sigma fixes it; G_sigma fixes exactly the trace-free vectors when
    75	sigma differs from 1. The independent check rebuilds the conformal
    76	projector as the group average (I + C + C^2)/3 of the 3-cycle C and
    77	reproduces all of it.
    78	
    79	Not established: that any physical sector ledger has this form, or
    80	any admissibility classification of graded operators.
    81	
    82	### 2. Affine grading normal form on the line w(t) = (1, 1+t, 1-t)
    83	
    84	Stipulated: the direction set D is the six unit vectors of Z^3 in the
    85	fixed order (+x, -x, +y, -y, +z, -z); a configuration is a direction
    86	d and a triple tau in D^3; the balance residual is
    87	r(t) = sum_s w_s(t) D[tau_s] - w_0(t) D[d] on the grading line
    88	w(t) = (1, 1+t, 1-t); the raw ledger is
    89	(D[tau_0] - D[d], D[tau_1], D[tau_2]) and its sector trace is the sum
    90	of its three vectors.
    91	
    92	Exact results, verified on all 1296 configurations (7776 residual
    93	identities at six rational probe points, and again by two-point
    94	interpolation at two fresh probe points in the independent check):
    95	r(t) = A + tB exactly, with A = D[tau_0] + D[tau_1] + D[tau_2] - D[d]
    96	a function of the support alone and B = D[tau_1] - D[tau_2] never
    97	depending on the direction or the first sector; the sector trace of
    98	the raw ledger is identically A.
    99	
   100	Not established: any census of lawful configurations, any retirement
   101	of the parameter t, and any claim about which grading is physical.
   102	
   103	### 3. The permutation module of C_3 on Q^3
   104	
   105	Stipulated: C is the permutation matrix of the 3-cycle
   106	(0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 0) acting on Q^3.
   107	
   108	Exact results: the fixed subspace is the line spanned by (1,1,1); the
   109	complement is C-invariant of dimension 2 with characteristic
   110	polynomial x^2 + x + 1, irreducible over Q (rational root theorem)
   111	and over R (negative discriminant), so the dimension pair over Q and
   112	over R is (1, 2); over C the module splits into three character
   113	lines, pattern (1, 1, 1). The independent check reproves this by
   114	character theory with exact arithmetic in Z[w]/(w^2 + w + 1): the
   115	multiplicities over C are (1, 1, 1) and the two nontrivial
   116	Galois-conjugate characters fuse into one 2-dimensional
   117	Q-irreducible.
   118	
   119	Not established: any identification of these dimensions with record
   120	weights, readout weights, formation weights, or any physical pair.
   121	The review found that identification to be an unproved bridge; it is
   122	removed here, not repaired.
   123	
   124	### 4. Five-form collapse, family coincidence at N = 3, and the fixed-locus sum
   125	
   126	Stipulated: the five closed forms in (w0, w1, n)
   127	
   128	    w1/(w0+w1)^2,  w0*w1/n^2,  w1/n^2,  (n-1)/n^2,  w1/(w0*n^2)
   129	
   130	on the locus (w0, w1) = (1, n-1); and the three rational families
   131	(N-1)/N^2, (N^2-1)/(12N), (N-1)(N-2)/(3N).
   132	
   133	Exact results: on the locus every one of the five forms equals
   134	(n-1)/n^2 — as values for n = 2..50 in the primary and as
   135	cross-multiplied polynomial identities in the independent check, so
   136	the five-fold "choice" among them is a choice of expression, not of
   137	value, on that locus. The three families coincide pairwise exactly at
   138	N = 3 (common value 2/9) and separate at every other N in 2..200
   139	(at N = 4 they read 3/16, 5/16, 1/2). The fixed-locus sum over the
   140	nontrivial N-th roots of unity z of 1/((1-z)(1-z^{-1})) equals
   141	(N^2-1)/12 exactly for N = 2..12, computed in the quotient ring
