   182	Not established: that any physical constant equals (n-1)/n^3, or that
   183	the structure prefers this witness over any other.
   184	
   185	### 7. Pointer-cycle identity
   186	
   187	Stipulated: G is a finite simple graph on labelled vertices with a
   188	marked vertex S.
   189	
   190	Exact result: a cycle through S exists iff two distinct neighbours of
   191	S are joined in G - S, and then the shortest cycle through S has
   192	length exactly 2 + min over distinct neighbour pairs (a, b) of S of
   193	the distance from a to b in G - S. Proof shape: any cycle through S
   194	runs S, a, ..., b, S with the inner path avoiding S, giving the lower
   195	bound; a shortest inner path closes to a simple cycle attaining it.
