RL_SALVAGE_FULL_PR5995.log:1282:{"baseRefName":"physics-loop/toe-time-blockAC1-20260802","baseRefOid":"3a01b7c0f7cc180cf043c3d38416cdce0c4b9a5c","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-08-05T04:07:34Z","authors":[{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-05T04:07:34Z","messageBody":"…-1 sweep corpus)\n\nVendored read-only source material for the Cycle 928 R-eta route-1 sweep.\n121 files across 16 packages. 83/83 files covered by a ship receipt were\ndigest-verified (sha256 + git blob) against that receipt; 0 mismatches.\n26 files from packages that HAVE NO SHIP RECEIPT ANYWHERE IN THE CAMPAIGN\n(cycles 872, 876, 882, 883) were verified against their originating branch\nblob instead; 0 mismatches. 12 ship receipts vendored alongside.\n\nSPEC DEVIATIONS / PLACEMENT CORRECTIONS (every placement verified with\ngit ls-tree + the package's own ship-receipt \"block\" field, not trusted):\n\n  - spec said the theta-core/sigma-split package (Cycle 903) is on blockG20\n    \"or a nearby G-branch\". It is on blockG26; its ship receipt records\n    block toe-time-blockG26-20260802. blockG20 carries Cycle 897 instead.\n  - spec said the unit-grading/owner-surface package is \"Cycle 883-ish\".\n    Cycle 883 is the RECORD WEIGHT PAIR package (blockG8). The unit-grading\n    package is Cycle 876 (blockG8) - a different cycle. Both vendored.\n  - spec said the k-run/period instrument (Cycle 891, blockT5) is already\n    vendored by 924. Confirmed present in this worktree; re-verified.\n  - the G-branches are NOT a linear chain: G8 IS an ancestor of G9/G10, but\n    G17 is not an ancestor of G18, G22 not of G23, G25 not of G26, G26 not\n    of G27. Each late G-branch is a sibling off a shared base. Every source\n    was therefore checked out from its OWN branch pin.\n\nFIREWALL QUARANTINE - deliberately NOT vendored (pinned by digest only):\n  - Cycle 897 (blockG20, target_integrity) - all 7 files carry PDG mass\n    literals by the package's own declaration (\"3 quarantined admitted\n    observations\").\n  - Cycle 923 (blockR1, exactness_residual) - all 7 files carry PDG mass\n    literals.\n  Both are still swept: pinned by sha256 + blob and triaged from typing\n  sentences that contain no numeric literals.\n\nOVERSIZE, pinned not vendored:\n  - outputs/loop_cost_cycle921_receipt_2026_07_28.json (3599 KiB).\n\nExact commands run in this worktree (branch pins resolved at vendor time):\n\n  git checkout 5fcaa4fe04 -- <cycle886 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG11\n  git checkout c00b3de3d4 -- <cycle888 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG13\n  git checkout be17159a6b -- <cycle890 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG14\n  git checkout 8754ce823e -- <cycle895 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG18\n  git checkout dde8a54d3e -- <cycle898 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG21\n  git checkout e2ebfd309d -- <cycle899 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG22\n  git checkout 98c280cdb5 -- <cycle900 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG23\n  git checkout d4eaf5d833 -- <cycle901 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG24\n  git checkout 99ba95df13 -- <cycle903 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG26\n  git checkout c099d9d215 -- <cycle904 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockG27\n  git checkout 7074766c6a -- <cycle916 ship receipt + 7 files>   # blockM3\n  git checkout 2db39dea9a -- <cycle921 ship receipt + 6 files>   # blockM7\n  git checkout da7e6d05cb -- <cycle872 note + 5 files>           # blockG3\n  git checkout f5f1cf9f0a -- <cycle876/882/883 notes + 17 files> # blockG8\n\nNothing here is authored by this cycle; no axiom, primitive, registry,\npolicy, queue, or audit surface is touched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"cycle928: vendor pinned angle-and-scale-carrying artifacts (the route…","oid":"d1d9e3bb8f2db5a497c5b30c32be0a1932abb5c4"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-05T04:19:13Z","authors":[{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-05T04:19:13Z","messageBody":"…new wall\n\nPASS=46 FAIL=0, 2.6s, deterministic double-run with identical science digest\n23e65049900519d9.\n\nRestriction gates cleared BEFORE any new number:\n  - the angle-native no-go runner reproduced, literal \"TOTAL: PASS=128 FAIL=0\"\n  - the stretch no-go reproduced at PASS=113 FAIL=0, re-confirming 924's audit\n    row 1 (the note's Verification section claims PASS>=120)\n  - Cycle 924's ship receipt digest-verified 7/7 and its science digest\n    ccd98a3916cc40d5 reproduced by re-running its own primary\n  - 83 vendored files digest-verified against their ship receipts, 0 mismatches\n\nRESULT. 18 candidates over 17 vendored packages (99 files) plus 1\nfirewall-quarantined package. ZERO survivors. But the blocking obstruction is\nNOT the one that killed route 3, and that is the finding:\n\n  - 924 killed route 3 with BIN 5, the referent gap: the occurrence surface had\n    no word for a lepton. That gate does NOT fire here. Ten of these packages\n    do carry charged-lepton / Koide / fixed-locus / S_sum vocabulary, and three\n    candidates derive a value that is EXACTLY 2/3 on a referent-carrying\n    surface -- Cycle 899's sum_of_inverse_determinants = 2/3 over the C3 fixed\n    locus is the sharpest R-eta candidate the campaign has produced.\n\n  - What stops all three is a NEW bin, BIN 7, the TYPE GAP: the entire new\n    surface contains ZERO occurrences of the word \"radian\" (99 files, 17\n    packages, positive-control scan proves the scanner is not blind). Every\n    derived object is a density, a determinant sum, a weight, a count or a\n    dimension. No artifact supplies a sentence converting any of them into an\n    angle -- and that missing sentence IS the h-unit angle scale that Cycle 924\n    computed as the one unpriced dimension. The two blocks meet on the same\n    object from opposite directions.\n\n  - Held in reserve, BIN 8, the SCOPE GAP: even granting the type conversion,\n    the 2/3 exists only at the C3 / n=3 scope, which this campaign's own\n    theorems prove is unselected -- 886 (0 of 16 routes grounded-and-isolating),\n    888 (freeness+maximality selects S3 alone over the 30-subgroup lattice),\n    890 (ladder endpoint {C3, C4}), 904 (442 families, 115 distinct values).\n\nEvery BIN 5 candidate also carries its secondary bin, per 924's discipline.\n\nTen teeth, all firing, including the two the spec demanded: a planted 2/3 by\nnumerology is caught by the typing gate, and a planted candidate that IS\nradian-typed, referent-carrying, scope-forced and derivably identified is\nACCEPTED as a SURVIVOR by the same code path -- so the empty sweep is a\nfinding, not a constant function.\n\nTwo self-found defects fixed in the open: `\\b` does not match between a digit\nand an underscore, which silently emptied the corpus scan; and the firewall\ndetector flagged its own pattern.\n\nNothing adopted. No axiom, primitive, registry, policy, queue or audit surface\ntouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"cycle928: primary runner -- R-eta route 1 swept, the TYPE GAP is the …","oid":"d43459a82d70f39a0b4be57c5a488bb84b51b6c2"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-05T04:20:53Z","authors":[{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-05T04:20:53Z","messageBody":"Self-found defect, fixed against interest: the referent gate counted raw\nsubstring hits, which inflated it three ways --\n\n  - corpus-scan HIT LISTS. Cycle 883 \"mentions\" Koide 5 times; all five are\n    filenames in a 10,145-file inventory sweep. Cycle 895's 19 Koide hits and\n    Cycle 901's 157 are the same thing. The package scanned a tree; it did not\n    talk about a lepton.\n  - cited NOTE FILENAMES, including the July no-go's own filename.\n  - substring artefacts: \"s_sum\" occurs inside \"dimensions_sum_to_the_orbit_\n    length\" (99 such in cycle 886 alone).\n\nThe gate now counts prose occurrences only and reports the path/filename and\nfalse-positive hits separately, so the classification is auditable rather than\nasserted. Effect: the packages carrying a genuine charged-lepton/fixed-locus\nreferent drop from 10 to 7 (882, 886, 888, 890, 898, 899, 901), and cycles 883\nand 895 move from \"referent present\" to bin 5 where they belong.\n\nThis makes the sweep HARDER on itself, not easier: an inflated referent gate\nwould have moved more candidates into bin 7 and made the type-gap finding look\nbroader than it is. The three candidates that clear both of route 3's killers\nare unchanged -- C899-SUM (sum_of_inverse_determinants = 2/3 over the C3 fixed\nlocus), C898-TRACE (per-vertex trace 2/3, rejected by its own source as\n\"RATIONAL BUT WRONG\") and C897-Q -- and all three are still stopped by the type\ngap alone.\n\nAlso replaced an arbitrary headcount assertion with the substantive one: the\nreferent gate must be a nonempty PROPER subset, which proves both that it still\ndiscriminates and that it no longer kills every candidate as it did on the\noccurrence surface.\n\nPASS=46 FAIL=0, 2.7s, deterministic double-run, science digest c171abf56be81d34.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"cycle928: tighten the referent gate to PROSE hits only","oid":"05eb0d528fe48b847790a14d5dbd82c48383484c"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-05T04:26:36Z","authors":[{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-05T04:26:36Z","messageBody":"… that hold\n\nVERDICT: PRIMARY_SURVIVES_THIS_CHECK. PASS=21 FAIL=0, 0.2s. Zero refutations\noverturn the conclusion. Fully independent: own corpus discovery by filename\nshape (not the primary's package table), own candidate pool built by exhaustive\nexact-rational extraction (not a curated anchor list), bin taxonomy re-derived\nfrom the JULY NO-GO'S OWN BYTES, own hasher, own gate reimplementation.\n\nTHE CHECKER CAUGHT A REAL DEFECT AND THE PRIMARY WAS FIXED:\n\n  ENUMERATION INCOMPLETENESS (held, now closed). The checker's independent\n  extraction found an exact 2/3 in cycle 901 that the primary's pool did not\n  anchor -- the diagonal of the projector onto the plane normal to the body\n  diagonal, on a surface that DOES carry the referent in prose. The primary now\n  enumerates it as C901-PROJDIAG; it lands in BIN 7 with the others, so the\n  verdict is unchanged but the census is complete. The attack now FAILS, which\n  is the correct end state.\n\nTHREE REFUTATIONS STILL HOLD, none overturning, all reported:\n\n  1. UNAVERAGED-SUM CONVENTION. Cycle 882's 2/9 candidate is binned \"misses the\n     target\", but under the no-go's OWN normalisation Phi = 3*L it is worth\n     exactly 2/3. The bin label is normalisation-dependent. It does not move the\n     verdict: the disputed step was never the factor of 3, it is reading the\n     result as radians -- bin 7 either way.\n  2. SCOPE. Cycles [857, 864, 868, 870, 871, 909, 911, 912, 913, 924] sit in this\n     worktree inside the campaign window and were NOT swept. \"Route 1 swept\n     empty\" is not a campaign-wide statement. The primary's HONEST SCOPE\n     sentence already says so, so the receipt does not overclaim -- but a reader\n     quoting the headline without it would.\n  3. REFERENT DEPTH. On cycles 886 and 888 the charged-lepton referent is ONE\n     sentence, imported verbatim from the cycle-882 primary, which both packages\n     themselves grade \"target-facing, not axiom-grounded\" and cite as a CIRCULAR\n     selector. They QUOTE the language, they do not derive in it. This narrows\n     the primary's finding rather than refuting it: a thinner referent pushes\n     candidates toward bin 5, also a non-survivor bin.\n\nA CHECKER SELF-DEFECT, found and fixed in the open: its first run reported 67\n\"radian\" hits and declared PRIMARY_REFUTED. All 90 were in cycle 928's OWN\nreceipts and caches -- the sweep reporting the absence of the word. The corpus\nnow excludes the artifact under test, and the exclusion is ASSERTED not assumed:\nCK11b requires that every radian occurrence in the campaign window belong to\ncycle 928, and it passes. No surveyed package uses the word.\n\nThe checker also found a bin-4 obstruction the primary had not cited and which\nSTRENGTHENS the no-survivor verdict: cycle 899's own independent checker records\nthat 402 closed forms return 2/9 at C3 while taking 10 distinct values at C4, so\nthe form producing the 2/3 sum is not singled out by the data. Carried as a new\naudit row, with the referent-depth finding.\n\nPrimary re-run after the fold-back: PASS=47 FAIL=0, 19 candidates, BIN 7 = 4.\nBoth runners deterministic across a double-run.\n\nThe gitignored audit ledger materialized read-only for the inherited gate\nrunners has been removed; nothing committed, no audit surface written.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"cycle928: independent checker -- 21 checks, 10 attacks, 3 refutations…","oid":"24049ea8dd9991a46a1927021cb964d4d735bc8c"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-05T04:28:57Z","authors":[{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-05T04:28:57Z","messageBody":"A deep read of the vendored corpus found the one thing the sweep had missed,\nand it makes the result sharper rather than weaker.\n\nTHE FINDING. Cycle 901's C901-T2a derives that a generator of a cyclic order-n\nrotation group \"acts on the normal plane as a rotation by 2 pi k / n\". That is\na genuine ANGLE -- the only genuinely angle-valued derived object anywhere on\nthe surfaces this campaign built -- and it sits on the C3 body diagonal, the\nvery cycle R-eta is about. It is now enumerated as C901-ROTANGLE and graded\nangle-typed AGAINST this block's interest: crediting it makes the type gap\nnarrower, not wider.\n\nAND IT MISSES, in the no-go's own already-closed bin. At n = 3 the angle is\n2*pi/3 -- a canonical 2*pi packaging of a rational, exactly what the July no-go\nexcluded (\"not 2*pi*S_sum\"). The miss is unbridgeable for the no-go's own\nstated reason: 2*pi*k/n = 2/3 would force pi = n/(3k), rational. So it cannot\nbe closed at any k or n.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS. The route-1 verdict is now a two-sided statement instead of a\nbare absence:\n  - the surface's one real ANGLE (2*pi/3) is not the target; and\n  - the surface's objects that ARE worth exactly 2/3 (899's\n    sum_of_inverse_determinants over the C3 fixed locus, 904's and 901's\n    projector diagonals, 898's per-vertex trace) are not angles.\nThe sentence that would join those two facts is precisely the missing h-unit\nangle-scale license that Cycle 924 computed as the one unpriced dimension.\n\"No angle exists\" was the weaker and slightly wrong claim; \"the angle exists,\nit is the wrong one, and it is wrong in a bin already closed in July\" is the\ntrue one.\n\nNEW AUDIT ROW 9: cycle 903's note claims its fidelity sweep returned \"15\nPARTIAL\"; its own receipt and runner cache both record 10. FAIL=0 either way\nand nothing here depends on the count. Reported, not repaired.\n\nPrimary PASS=48 FAIL=0, 2.7s. Checker PASS=21 FAIL=0,\nPRIMARY_SURVIVES_THIS_CHECK, 3 refutations hold, 0 overturn. Both deterministic\nacross a double-run. The gitignored audit ledger materialized read-only for the\ninherited gate runners has been removed; nothing committed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"cycle928: the surface has exactly ONE angle, and it is 2*pi/3 -- not 2/3","oid":"0fed08212e834c9572f80e25c9bd61fe5e6f1e5c"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-05T04:32:19Z","authors":[{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-05T04:32:19Z","messageBody":"…ipt)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"ph